{"tool_name":"astral-pro_2","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"astral-pro_2","home":"https://github.com/chaoszhang/ASTER","license":"AGPL-3.0","summary":"Accurate Species Tree EstimatoR series: a family of optimation algorithms for species tree inference implemented in C++ (including ASTRAL-Pro & Weighted ASTRAL)","addition_date":"2022-10-26T09:22:19.621090Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:26:06.617858Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:astral-pro_2","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"smirarab@ucsd.edu","name":"Siavash Mirarab","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Chao Zhang"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Phylogenetic reconstruction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3478"}]}],"name":"ASTRAL-Pro 2","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac620","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Species tree inference from multi-copy gene trees has long been a challenge in phylogenomics. The recent method ASTRAL-Pro has made strides by enabling multi-copy gene family trees as input and has been quickly adopted. Yet, its scalability, especially memory usage, needs to improve to accommodate the ever-growing dataset size. Results: We present ASTRAL-Pro 2, an ultrafast and memory efficient version of ASTRAL-Pro that adopts a placement-based optimization algorithm for significantly better scalability without sacrificing accuracy.","authors":[{"name":"Mirarab S."},{"name":"Zhang C."}],"citationCount":15,"date":"2022-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"ASTRAL-Pro 2: ultrafast species tree reconstruction from multi-copy gene family trees"},"pmid":"36094339"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene and protein families","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0623"},{"term":"Phylogenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0194"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"ASTRAL-Pro 2","home":"https://bio.tools/